cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "A Decision-Support Framework for Evaluating Urban Greening under Water–Energy Constraints in Desalination-Dependent Cities"

message: "If you use this software, please cite both the accompanying publication and this repository."

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Almaktoum
    given-names: Nelly F.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9887-0280"

repository-code: "https://github.com/nelmkt/NEGI-Framework"

license: MIT

version: "1.0.0"

abstract: >
  An open-source Python framework for evaluating urban greening strategies
  under coupled water–energy constraints using satellite remote sensing,
  machine learning, spatial validation, uncertainty analysis, and the
  Normalized Environmental Gain Index (NEGI).

keywords:
  - Normalized Environmental Gain Index
  - NEGI
  - Urban Heat Island
  - Urban Greening
  - Remote Sensing
  - Machine Learning
  - XGBoost
  - Land Surface Temperature
  - Spatial Validation
  - Google Earth Engine
  - Desalination
  - Sustainability
